# How long does sunlight take to reach Earth?
subtitle: "Guess how many minutes sunlight takes to reach Earth, then see why you always see the Sun as it was, and how old its light really is."

## How long does sunlight take to reach Earth?
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: nasa
      title: 'Sun: facts; How long does it take sunlight to reach the Earth?'
      authors: NASA
      year: 2024
      finding: sunlight crosses the 150 million km to Earth in about 8 minutes 20 seconds; energy from the core takes about 170,000 years to reach the surface (estimates range from about 10,000 to a million years); moonlight reaches Earth in about 1.3 seconds

    card title "How long does sunlight take to reach us?"

Light is the fastest thing there is, three hundred thousand kilometres every second. And the Sun is a hundred and fifty million kilometres away.
    icon sun size 300 set twemoji x 210 y 470 icon_look picture of sun
    icon earth size 170 set twemoji x 830 y 470 icon_look picture of "globe showing europe-africa"
    scale mins cites ["nasa"] x 100 y 235 width 800 unit min min 0 max 20 value 8.3 ticks 4
    parallel true

    ask "How many minutes does sunlight take to reach the Earth? Click on the line." on mins store t default "2"
        right: Close: you said {t} minutes, and it is about {t.true}.
        wrong: You said {t} minutes; it is about {t.true}.

    erase mins mins_answer

So even light needs eight minutes and twenty seconds to cross the gap.
    arrow beam dashed #d89b1c from.x 370 from.y 470 to.x 735 to.y 470 style.stroke_width 4
    text t_res "8 min 20 s" #b5482e cites ["nasa"] x 550 y 530 font_size 56

When you glance at the Sun, you see it as it was eight minutes ago.
    text ago "8 minutes ago" #2f6b8f x 210 y 285 font_size 40

If it vanished this instant, the sky would stay bright for eight more minutes before anyone on Earth could know.
    fade sun to 0.2 duration 2

    fade sun to 1 duration 0.5

Moonlight is quicker. It is sunlight bounced off the Moon, and covers the last stretch to us in just over a second.
    icon moon size 110 set twemoji x 830 y 240 icon_look picture of "crescent moon"
    arrow moon_arrow #2f6b8f from.x 830 from.y 300 to.x 830 to.y 380
    text moon_l "1.3 s" #2f6b8f x 930 y 340 font_size 40

    erase ago

But sunlight is old long before it sets out, because it starts deep inside the Sun.
    path walk thick #b5482e points [[210,470],[200,539],[173,494],[261,416],[143,520],[206,459],[189,520],[278,540],[261,501],[178,459],[178,533],[239,403],[156,440],[150,477],[147,468],[261,499],[249,501],[300,470]]

The energy made in the core bounces around in there for tens of thousands of years, maybe far more, before it reaches the surface.
    text inside "~170,000 years" #b5482e cites ["nasa"] x 210 y 285 font_size 44

And then the final dash to your eyes takes just eight minutes.
    point at.ref t_res gesture underline

